        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What should you look for when choosing a psychologist in Famagusta?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">Because the options on the island are limited, people often go to the first place they find. A few things are worth checking first: that the psychologist is licensed, which age groups they work with, which language sessions will be held in, and whether you can realistically get to the centre regularly.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">In most places the first meeting is an introduction and is not binding. If it did not feel right, saying so is ordinary — what most determines whether therapy works is the relationship that gets built.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

