        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">If you are an international student</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Famagusta is a university town, and students arrive with their own set of reasons: exam anxiety, adjusting to the island, being far from family, workload, uncertainty after graduation. Sessions in English matter here, and they are available.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong class="text-ink font-medium">If you are a currently enrolled student at Eastern Mediterranean University</strong>, the university's own Psychological Counselling, Guidance and Research Centre (PDRAM) is on campus and <strong class="text-ink font-medium">free of charge</strong>. We would suggest looking there first.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Coming to us makes sense when you are not a student, after you graduate, if you are at another university, if you would prefer somewhere independent of your university, or if you want continuity. More detail: <a href="/en/services/student-counselling.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">Student counselling</a></p>
